+## Recovery snapshot recording
+
+`progress.md` is one versioned current snapshot plus human-readable progress
+rendered from that snapshot. It is not a second event journal. Record through
+`record-recovery.mjs` so evidence is retained and fsynced before
+acknowledgment. The receipt is `{acknowledged, revision, eventId,
+snapshotEvidence, retained, evidence, progressPath}`. Reconcile a lost ack
+by reading `eventId` (`sjujperpowers:record:<plan-key>:r<revision>`) and the
+published `snapshotEvidence`.
+
+Initialize (workflow `sdd` or `inline`; `session` must persist todos):
+
+```bash
+node <tracking-providers skill dir>/scripts/record-recovery.mjs \
+  --root "$(jj root)" \
+  --plan docs/project/plans/feature.md \
+  --event '{"workflow":"sdd","expectedRevision":1,"current":{"task":1,"phase":"implement","round":null,"nextAction":"implement task 1"},"todos":[{"id":"t1","content":"Task 1","status":"in_progress"}]}'
+```
+
+Finding, ruling, fix round, completion, and inline todos:
+
+```json
+{"type":"finding","finding":{"id":"f1","task":2,"status":"open","summary":"missing progress reporting","evidence":[]},"current":{"task":2,"phase":"fix","round":1,"nextAction":"resume fix round 1"}}
+{"type":"decision","decision":{"id":"d1","task":2,"summary":"keep the helper","rationale":"spec requires it","costIfWrong":"rework the helper","sourceText":"Ruling: keep the helper — spec requires it — rework the helper","evidence":[]}}
+{"type":"fix-round","task":2,"round":1,"expectedRevision":3,"findings":[{"id":"f1","task":2,"status":"open","summary":"missing progress reporting","evidence":[]}],"rejectedApproaches":[{"id":"r1","task":2,"summary":"rewrite from scratch","reason":"loses the reviewed interface","evidence":[]}]}
+{"type":"complete-task","task":2,"expectedRevision":4,"changes":{"base":"<commit>","head":"<commit>"}}
+{"workflow":"inline","todos":[{"id":"t2","content":"Task 2","status":"in_progress"}],"current":{"task":2,"phase":"execute","round":null,"nextAction":"execute task 2"}}
+```
+
+Failure/recovery rules:
+
+- Validate the event, expected revision, and plan digest before any
+  destructive write. Exact `evidenceRefs` must already verify; same-length
+  mutated bytes are rejected.
+- Copy referenced bytes into `retained/` before replacing the current
+  snapshot. Do not hardlink. Do not keep checkpoints on mutable report paths.
+- Kata enrollment requires a mapping for every plan task, live `issue.revision`
+  (integer), `issue.status`, `sjujperpowers.plan` / `sjujperpowers.task`
+  metadata, `sjujperpowers-task` labels, and lease/owner identity from show.
